        "worked_solution": "First, recall the following:\n\n- ${J}_{1}(-7)$ represents a $1\\times 1$ Jordan block with $-7$'s on the leading diagonal,\n\n- ${J}_{2}(-2)$ represents a $2\\times 2$ Jordan block with $-2$'s on the leading diagonal.\n\nTherefore, our Jordan blocks are given by\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(-7)=[\\begin{aligned}-7\\end{aligned}],\\,{J}_{2}(-2)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe composition of our Jordan blocks gives the following block diagonal matrix:\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(-7)\\,\u2295\\,{J}_{2}(-2)=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
